# Sample requests for every endpoint of the API (design section 4), as one walk-through of the main flow:
# sign in -> master data -> receive -> order -> send -> complementary -> complete -> notifications -> returns
# -> adjustments -> users -> (v1.1) a Seller -> customers -> sales orders and open demand -> ship -> reports
# -> cancel and delete.
#
# Tools: the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or the .http editor of Visual Studio 2022 17.12 or later. Both send
# the request under the cursor ("Send Request") and both support the variables used here:
#   - file variables (@host = ...), used as {{host}};
#   - request variables: "# @name signIn" names a request, and {{signIn.response.body.$.accessToken}} reads a field
#     of its last response. So run the requests in order, top to bottom: each one uses ids from the ones above.
#
# Start the API first (architecture section 8): dotnet run --project src/InventoryTracker.Api
# The walk-through creates units, items and users with fixed names, so it runs once against a fresh database.
# To start again: stop the app and delete src/InventoryTracker.Api/inventory.db*.
#
# Development only. Port 5133 is also the default port of the Production API started by scripts\run.ps1, so check
# which one is running before you send anything: the walk-through writes data, and records are never deleted
# (PRD section 5). Never run it against the real database.
#
# Passwords: never type a real password into this file, because it is tracked by git. Every password below is
# read with {{$dotenv ...}} from a file named .env in this folder (src/InventoryTracker.Api/.env), which .gitignore
# already excludes, NOT from a .env at the repository root. Create it with these six lines (the names are also in
# the repository's .env.example), replacing each placeholder with a value of your own:
#   ADMIN_EMAIL=owner@example.com
#   ADMIN_PASSWORD=<choose-your-own-strong-password>
#   SAMPLE_USER_PASSWORD=<choose-a-password-for-the-sample-user>
#   SAMPLE_USER_RESET_PASSWORD=<choose-a-second-password>
#   SAMPLE_USER_NEW_PASSWORD=<choose-a-third-password>
#   SAMPLE_SELLER_PASSWORD=<choose-a-password-for-the-sample-seller>
# ADMIN_EMAIL and ADMIN_PASSWORD are the first Manager's, the values you stored with dotnet user-secrets
# (architecture section 8). The three SAMPLE_USER_ passwords are for the Warehouse user that section 11 creates,
# resets and then changes, and (v1.1) SAMPLE_SELLER_PASSWORD is for the Seller user that section 12 creates and
# signs in as. Each must pass the policy (8+ characters, an upper-case letter, a lower-case letter and a digit),
# and the three SAMPLE_USER_ ones must differ. The app itself never reads .env; the file is only for these sample
# requests. Both editors support $dotenv. Every email below is a placeholder.

@host = http://localhost:5133
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### Health check (anonymous): answers "Healthy" when the app and its database are up.
GET {{host}}/health

### OpenAPI description (anonymous, Development only): every endpoint, its shapes, status codes and the Bearer scheme.
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

###
# ---- 1. Sign in (US-01) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Sign in as the first Manager. Every later request sends the returned token (valid for 8 hours).
# @name signIn
POST {{api}}/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_EMAIL}}", "password": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_PASSWORD}}" }

###
@token = {{signIn.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
# ---- 2. Master data: units, items, recipes (US-06, US-07, US-08) -------------------------------------------------

### Create the unit "kg" (Manager).
# @name createKg
POST {{api}}/units
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "kg" }

###
@kgId = {{createKg.response.body.$.id}}

### Create the unit "bag" (renamed below).
# @name createBag
POST {{api}}/units
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "bag" }

###
@bagId = {{createBag.response.body.$.id}}

### List units, newest first (any role). Every list takes page (default 1) and pageSize (1 to 100, default 50).
GET {{api}}/units?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One unit.
GET {{api}}/units/{{kgId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rename a unit (Manager): "bag" becomes "Bag". A unit's own current name never counts as taken.
PUT {{api}}/units/{{bagId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bag" }

### Create a unit to delete next.
# @name createBox
POST {{api}}/units
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Box" }

### Delete a unit that no item uses (Manager): 204.
DELETE {{api}}/units/{{createBox.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create the raw material Cheese, measured in kg.
# @name createCheese
POST {{api}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cheese", "description": "Mozzarella, 20 kg blocks", "type": "RawMaterial", "unitId": {{kgId}} }

###
@cheeseId = {{createCheese.response.body.$.id}}

### Create the finished product, counted in bags.
# @name createProduct
POST {{api}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Shredded cheese 1 kg bag", "description": "Mozzarella blend, retail pack", "type": "FinishedProduct", "unitId": {{bagId}} }

###
@productId = {{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### List raw materials only (filter: type).
GET {{api}}/items?type=RawMaterial
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One item.
GET {{api}}/items/{{cheeseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace an item (all four fields). Type and unit can change only while the item is not in use.
PUT {{api}}/items/{{cheeseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cheese", "description": "Mozzarella, 20 kg blocks, chilled", "type": "RawMaterial", "unitId": {{kgId}} }

### Create an item to delete next.
# @name createSpare
POST {{api}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Spare label roll", "type": "RawMaterial", "unitId": {{kgId}} }

### Delete an item that has no movements, recipe lines or order lines (Manager): 204.
DELETE {{api}}/items/{{createSpare.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Set the product's recipe: 1 kg of Cheese per bag (Manager). Replaces the whole list.
PUT {{api}}/items/{{productId}}/recipe
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lines": [ { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "amountPerUnit": 1 } ] }

### Read the recipe.
GET {{api}}/items/{{productId}}/recipe
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ---- 3. Receive stock; read stock and movements (US-09, US-10, US-11) --------------------------------------------

### Record a receipt of 1,200 kg of Cheese into the Warehouse (Warehouse or Manager). 201 with the movement.
# @name receipt
POST {{api}}/receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "quantity": 1200, "receiptDate": "2026-11-01", "note": "Delivery note 4471" }

### Current stock of every item (filter: itemType).
GET {{api}}/stock?itemType=RawMaterial
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stock of one item, with committed amount, pending returns and free leftover.
GET {{api}}/stock/{{cheeseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Movement history (filters: itemId, location, type, orderNumber, complementaryOrderNumber, from, to).
GET {{api}}/movements?itemId={{cheeseId}}&type=Received
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One movement: the receipt above (its Location header points here).
GET {{api}}/movements/{{receipt.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ---- 4. Production order: create, view (US-13, US-14) ------------------------------------------------------------

### Create an order for 1,000 bags (Manager). The detail shows each line's estimate and send range.
# @name createOrder
POST {{api}}/production-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "finishedProductId": {{productId}}, "orderedQuantity": 1000 }

###
@orderNumber = {{createOrder.response.body.$.number}}

### List orders (filter: status).
GET {{api}}/production-orders?status=Created
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One order, by number.
GET {{api}}/production-orders/{{orderNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ---- 5. Send materials (US-15) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Send 1,000 kg of Cheese (Warehouse or Manager). Every line once; within the range shown on the order (980 to 1,020).
POST {{api}}/production-orders/{{orderNumber}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lines": [ { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "quantity": 1000 } ] }

###
# ---- 6. Complementary orders (US-16, US-17, US-18) ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Request 20 kg more for the running order (Production or Manager). Raises a notification for Managers.
# @name requestComplementary
POST {{api}}/production-orders/{{orderNumber}}/complementary-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Hopper spill at start of run", "lines": [ { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "requestedAmount": 20 } ] }

###
@complementaryNumber = {{requestComplementary.response.body.$.number}}

### List complementary orders (filters: status, orderNumber).
GET {{api}}/complementary-orders?orderNumber={{orderNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One complementary order.
GET {{api}}/complementary-orders/{{complementaryNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approve it (Manager). No body.
POST {{api}}/complementary-orders/{{complementaryNumber}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Send it (Warehouse or Manager), within its range (19.6 to 20.4).
POST {{api}}/complementary-orders/{{complementaryNumber}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lines": [ { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "quantity": 20 } ] }

### Request a second one, to reject next.
# @name requestSecond
POST {{api}}/production-orders/{{orderNumber}}/complementary-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Second spill", "lines": [ { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "requestedAmount": 5 } ] }

### Reject it (Manager). The note is optional; the body may be left out.
POST {{api}}/complementary-orders/{{requestSecond.response.body.$.number}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Use the spare from the last order" }

###
# ---- 7. Complete the order; cancel another (US-19, US-20, US-21) -------------------------------------------------

### Complete the order (Production or Manager): 1,001 bags made, 4 kg of Cheese left. The response shows the variances.
POST {{api}}/production-orders/{{orderNumber}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "producedQuantity": 1001, "lines": [ { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "leftover": 4 } ], "reason": "Last bag line jammed" }

### Create a second order, to cancel next.
# @name createSecondOrder
POST {{api}}/production-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "finishedProductId": {{productId}}, "orderedQuantity": 50 }

### Cancel it (Manager), with a reason.
POST {{api}}/production-orders/{{createSecondOrder.response.body.$.number}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Customer order withdrawn" }

###
# ---- 8. Notifications (US-23, Manager only) ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Unread notifications, newest first (filter: unreadOnly).
# @name notifications
GET {{api}}/notifications?unreadOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@notificationId = {{notifications.response.body.$.items[0].id}}

### One notification.
GET {{api}}/notifications/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark it read: 204.
POST {{api}}/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark every notification read: 204.
POST {{api}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ---- 9. Leftover returns (US-22) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Instruct a return of 3 kg of the leftover Cheese to the Warehouse (Manager). orderNumber is optional.
# @name instructReturn
POST {{api}}/returns
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "quantity": 3, "reason": "Not needed this week", "orderNumber": {{orderNumber}} }

###
@returnNumber = {{instructReturn.response.body.$.number}}

### List returns (filters: status, itemId).
GET {{api}}/returns?status=Pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One return.
GET {{api}}/returns/{{returnNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Record receiving it in the Warehouse (Warehouse or Manager). No body.
POST {{api}}/returns/{{returnNumber}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Instruct a second return, to cancel next.
# @name secondReturn
POST {{api}}/returns
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "quantity": 1, "reason": "Instructed by mistake" }

### Cancel it (Manager). No body.
POST {{api}}/returns/{{secondReturn.response.body.$.number}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ---- 10. Adjustments (US-12, Manager only) -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Write off 2 kg of spoiled Cheese in the Warehouse. 201 with the Adjustment movement.
POST {{api}}/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "location": "Warehouse", "quantity": -2, "reason": "Spoiled" }

###
# ---- 11. Users and passwords (US-03, US-04, Manager only except change-password) ---------------------------------

### Create a Warehouse user.
# @name createUser
POST {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "warehouse.user@example.com", "password": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_USER_PASSWORD}}", "roles": ["Warehouse"] }

###
@userId = {{createUser.response.body.$.id}}

### List users.
GET {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One user.
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Replace the user's roles. New roles apply from their next sign-in.
PUT {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["Warehouse", "Production"] }

### Deactivate the user: their tokens stop working at once.
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reactivate the user. They sign in again.
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reset the user's password: 204.
PUT {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newPassword": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_USER_RESET_PASSWORD}}" }

### Sign in as that user with the new password.
# @name signInUser
POST {{api}}/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "warehouse.user@example.com", "password": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_USER_RESET_PASSWORD}}" }

### Change your own password (any role): 204. Done as the new user, so the Manager's token above keeps working.
POST {{api}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{signInUser.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_USER_RESET_PASSWORD}}", "newPassword": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_USER_NEW_PASSWORD}}" }

###
# ==== v1.1 ========================================================================================================
# The version 1.1 walk-through (sales orders, customers, the Seller role). It runs after sections 1 to 11 and sells
# their finished product: the order completed in section 7 put 1,001 bags of "Shredded cheese 1 kg bag" in the
# Warehouse, and sections 3 to 10 left 181 kg of Cheese there. A Seller, created first, does everything a Seller may
# do: customers, sales orders, stock, reports and cancelling. The first Manager's token ({{token}}, section 1) ships
# and reads the movements, because those need the Warehouse or Manager role (design section 4); a Seller gets 403.

###
# ---- 12. (v1.1) A Seller user (US-03, US-30; Manager only) ------------------------------------------------------

### Create a Seller-only user (Manager). Its password is SAMPLE_SELLER_PASSWORD from .env (see the top of this file). 201.
# @name createSeller
POST {{api}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "seller.user@example.com", "password": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_SELLER_PASSWORD}}", "roles": ["Seller"] }

### Sign in as the Seller: 200 with the Seller's token, which sections 13, 14, 16 and 17 send.
# @name signInSeller
POST {{api}}/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "seller.user@example.com", "password": "{{$dotenv SAMPLE_SELLER_PASSWORD}}" }

###
@sellerToken = {{signInSeller.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
# ---- 13. (v1.1) Customers (US-29; changes: Manager or Seller; reads: Warehouse, Manager or Seller) ---------------

### Create the customer "Deli Norte" (Seller). Notes are optional, up to 500 characters. 201, active.
# @name createCustomer
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Deli Norte", "notes": "Deliveries before 10:00, ask for the kitchen." }

###
@customerId = {{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}

### Create a second customer, "Cafe Sur". 201.
# @name createCafeSur
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cafe Sur" }

###
@cafeSurId = {{createCafeSur.response.body.$.id}}

### List customers, newest first. Optional filter: isActive=true or false. 200: Cafe Sur, then Deli Norte.
GET {{api}}/customers?isActive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### One customer. 200.
GET {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Rename the customer and replace its notes (full replacement: leaving notes out clears them). 200, "Deli Norte SA".
PUT {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Deli Norte SA", "notes": "Deliveries before 10:00, ask for the kitchen." }

### Deactivate the customer: 200, isActive false; a new sales order for it would then get 409 customer-inactive. Repeating it
# succeeds and changes nothing.
POST {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Reactivate the customer, so section 14 can sell to it. 200, isActive true.
POST {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Create "Pizzeria Lago" by mistake; section 17 deletes it. 201.
# @name createMistake
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Pizzeria Lago" }

###
# ---- 14. (v1.1) Sales orders and open demand (US-24, US-25, US-31; create: Manager or Seller; reads: Warehouse,
# Manager or Seller; stock: any role) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a sales order for Deli Norte SA (Seller): 600 bags of the finished product and 120 kg of Cheese (any item
# type may be sold). customerReference is optional, up to 100 characters. 201, Created. Stock is not checked or moved.
# @name createSalesOrder
POST {{api}}/sales-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": {{customerId}}, "customerReference": "PO-2291", "lines": [ { "itemId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 600 }, { "itemId": {{cheeseId}}, "quantity": 120 } ] }

###
@salesOrderNumber = {{createSalesOrder.response.body.$.number}}

### Create a sales order for Cafe Sur (Seller): 1,200 bags, more than the Warehouse holds. 201 all the same: a sales
# order can be recorded before the stock exists (AC-24.2); the stock is checked only when it ships (section 15).
# @name createLargeSalesOrder
POST {{api}}/sales-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": {{cafeSurId}}, "lines": [ { "itemId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 1200 } ] }

###
@largeSalesOrderNumber = {{createLargeSalesOrder.response.body.$.number}}

### List sales orders, newest first. Optional filters, combined: status (Created, Shipped, Cancelled), itemId,
# customerId. 200: the Deli Norte SA sales order only.
GET {{api}}/sales-orders?status=Created&customerId={{customerId}}&itemId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### One sales order: the customer's current name, the lines with item type and unit, and the status history. 200.
GET {{api}}/sales-orders/{{salesOrderNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Stock of the finished products, with open demand (the quantity on Created sales orders; information only).
# 200: the bag row has warehouse 1001 and openDemand 1800 (600 + 1,200).
GET {{api}}/stock?itemType=FinishedProduct
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Stock of Cheese. 200: warehouse 181, openDemand 120.
GET {{api}}/stock/{{cheeseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

###
# ---- 15. (v1.1) Ship (US-26, US-28; Warehouse or Manager, so the first Manager's token) ------------------------

### Ship the Cafe Sur sales order. No quantities: every line ships in full, so 1,200 bags are needed and the Warehouse
# has 1,001. 409 insufficient-stock, "Not enough stock: Shredded cheese 1 kg bag in Warehouse has 1,001 Bag; sales
# order #{number} needs 1,200 Bag." (one sentence per short line). Nothing ships; it stays Created.
POST {{api}}/sales-orders/{{largeSalesOrderNumber}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ship the Deli Norte SA sales order: both lines are covered. The note is optional, up to 500 characters, and the
# body may be left out. 200, Shipped; one ShippedToCustomer movement per line. The Warehouse now holds 401 bags and
# 61 kg of Cheese.
POST {{api}}/sales-orders/{{salesOrderNumber}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Delivery note 8812" }

### The shipment's movements (Warehouse, Production or Manager). 200: two ShippedToCustomer movements, warehouseChange
# -600 (bags) and -120 (kg), both at the same time.
GET {{api}}/movements?salesOrderNumber={{salesOrderNumber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ---- 16. (v1.1) Shipped-totals reports (US-32, US-33; Warehouse, Manager or Seller) -----------------------------
# Totals of Shipped sales orders only, by shipment time; Created and Cancelled sales orders and adjustments never count,
# so the Cafe Sur sales order is left out. from and to are optional whole UTC days, both included (yyyy-MM-dd); with
# neither the period is all time, which is used here because the shipment above happened today. Rows are ordered by
# name, A to Z, not newest first, and paged as every list (page, pageSize).

### Shipped per item: one row per item with its type, unit, shipped quantity and number of sales orders. Optional
# filters, combined: from, to, itemType (RawMaterial or FinishedProduct), customerId. For one month, add for example
# from=2026-12-01&to=2026-12-31. 200, two rows: Cheese 120 kg, 1 sales order; Shredded cheese 1 kg bag 600 Bag, 1.
GET {{api}}/reports/shipped-by-item
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Shipped per customer and item, with the customer's current name and active status. Optional filters, combined:
# from, to, customerId, itemId. There is no total across items, because items have different units. 200, two rows,
# both Deli Norte SA: Cheese 120 kg, then Shredded cheese 1 kg bag 600 Bag, each 1 sales order.
GET {{api}}/reports/shipped-by-customer?customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

###
# ---- 17. (v1.1) Cancel a sales order; delete customers (US-27, US-29; Manager or Seller) ------------------------

### Cancel the Cafe Sur sales order (Seller). The reason is required, 1 to 500 characters. 200, Cancelled, with
# cancellationReason and a Cancelled history entry; no stock moves. A Shipped sales order (such as the Deli Norte SA
# one) gets 409 already-shipped; one already cancelled gets 409 sales-order-cancelled.
POST {{api}}/sales-orders/{{largeSalesOrderNumber}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Cafe Sur ordered more than we can supply; the order is withdrawn" }

### The bag's stock again. 200: warehouse 401, openDemand 0 (the only Created sales order is now Cancelled).
GET {{api}}/stock/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Delete Pizzeria Lago, which never had a sales order. 204.
DELETE {{api}}/customers/{{createMistake.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### Delete Deli Norte SA, which has a sales order (in any status, here Shipped). 409 customer-has-sales-orders,
# "Deli Norte SA has sales orders and cannot be deleted. Deactivate it instead."
DELETE {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
